From 060ab18a7ff7dc6e8232a4fb3ff3c81cb5f77b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yeasah Pell <yeasah@schwide.net>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:26:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Media] Chunk the vision-tower MLP over the token dimension

SHELVED -- correct and bit-exact, but it does not move the profiled peak on
any model measured. Kept because it becomes load-bearing the moment the
attention preamble is fixed. See the reactivation condition below.

A vision tower's MLP is pointwise over tokens, so slicing the forward into
row-chunks is bit-for-bit identical and bounds a buffer that otherwise scales
with the image's patch count. The chunk is derived from a byte budget
(VLLM_MM_ENCODER_MLP_CHUNK_MB, default 256) rather than being a row count, so
one setting holds across towers whose intermediate widths differ 3x: 10394
rows for so400m's 4304, 3266 for GLM-4.1V's 13696 gated to 27392.

Verified equivalent: 49152 rows in 16 chunks, torch.equal against the
single-shot path, max abs diff 0.0. Verified to fire in a real serve
("Chunking vision MLP: 48672 rows in 72 chunks of <=682").

WHY IT IS SHELVED. It shrinks the largest single *allocation* but not the
*peak*, and those are different quantities. On Qwen3.8's tower at 65536 rows
the MLP's 538 MiB activation buffer disappears -- it is exactly the
564,133,888 bytes the original OOM message named -- yet peak live memory is
1.728 GiB with or without chunking, because that buffer is never live at the
same instant as the peak. The peak is set by the attention preamble, where
q/k/v are materialized several times over at once: qkv gemm output, three
.contiguous() copies, then the rotary's output with the earlier copies still
live. Same on GLM-4.1V: 1.856 GiB either way. The OOM named the MLP because
that was the allocation that happened to fail after memory was already gone,
not because it was the cause.

REACTIVATION CONDITION. The MLP binds once the attention preamble's peak
drops below its 538 MiB single allocation (Qwen3.8 at full resolution; scale
by rows * 2 * intermediate_size * 2 for other towers). Until then this is
inert, so it stays off the appliance branch rather than diverging four files
for nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
